            "text": "{\"title\":\"Ethiopian Seafood Wat with Shrimp and Tilapia\",\"readyInMinutes\":45,\"servings\":4,\"summary\":\"This fragrant \u003cb\u003eEthiopian seafood wat\u003c/b\u003e delivers an exceptional blend of traditional Horn of Africa spices paired with delicate ocean flavors. Anchored by a robust base of slow-cooked red onions and aromatic \u003cb\u003eberbere spice blend\u003c/b\u003e, this vibrant stew reimagines classic regional cooking techniques for seafood lovers. Fresh wild shrimp and flaky tilapia fillets absorb the rich, complex gravy enriched with traditional \u003cb\u003eniter kibbeh\u003c/b\u003e, garlic, and freshly grated ginger. The resulting stew offers a satisfying balance of fiery heat, rich depth, and bright citrus accents from fresh lemon juice. Served traditionally alongside warm, spongy injera bread or steamed rice, this hearty main dish provides a wonderful introduction to coastal-style Ethiopian cuisine. Beyond its bold flavor profile, the meal is packed with lean protein, essential omega-3 fatty acids, and vibrant antioxidant-rich spices that make it both wholesome and indulgence-worthy. Perfect for weekend dinner gatherings or special cultural culinary explorations, this recipe brings a unique \u003cb\u003eseafood-forward twist\u003c/b\u003e to classic East African comfort food that will impress family and guests alike.\",\"nutrition\":{\"nutrients\":[{\"name\":\"Calories\",\"amount\":410,\"unit\":\"kcal\",\"percentOfDailyNeeds\":20.5},{\"name\":\"Fat\",\"amount\":16,\"unit\":\"g\",\"percentOfDailyNeeds\":20.5},{\"name\":\"Saturated Fat\",\"amount\":7,\"unit\":\"g\",\"percentOfDailyNeeds\":35},{\"name\":\"Carbohydrates\",\"amount\":18,\"unit\":\"g\",\"percentOfDailyNeeds\":6.5},{\"name\":\"Sugar\",\"amount\":6,\"unit\":\"g\",\"percentOfDailyNeeds\":6.7},{\"name\":\"Protein\",\"amount\":48,\"unit\":\"g\",\"percentOfDailyNeeds\":96},{\"name\":\"Cholesterol\",\"amount\":210,\"unit\":\"mg\",\"percentOfDailyNeeds\":70},{\"n